é\ª]==|„∫º´Êf;=øÜ<≈T(º¸˘4ºæ{=◊Rwª«˙øºQ©9-qä<∑¿␀ΩÄ/Í<(f≈ºÌÖ;˘SùºQJ∂;à÷<æ£KºßÅÄ<G¯;Dz;~ùºËPΩÙMº©ΩÛ	>iü;&<bRáª{≥ª˚≠ºï:\Væ;<ŒÇΩˆô<˜≠<›?ƒª÷T∫+ﬂËπÚìƒºZø"∫ﬁ!LºU•a8␀Fd<¨™vºÇªäÜﬁªCòñ<˛üL=$Ì!<%œ©ºH’…º¶ö7<ò8~;c4èºÙÃªıd<!AªEM*=.S=¢?ªâöõ<]8∆;êdØº¥3†;\e∫ºY›Ω4JΩ}¨ª‘œºÏ˚<ó$ºúW␀ºrõB<ç‹Ω”ËO<Dk"Ωsd=Ìeª¯≤ˇºK]È:·ãÛª°ûÓº“$¿<€ä∞;Ü:Ø<“ù;ì˚ <yLüª≤~å;{"title": "PACIENTE PEDI\u00c1TRICO:The entity \"PACIENTE PEDI\u00c1TRICO\" refers to children and adolescents who may require medical attention, particularly in the context of nutritional support. These patients often receive parenteral nutrition due to various medical conditions that put them at risk for metabolic and nutritional complications. Parenteral nutrition is a critical intervention for pediatric patients who cannot obtain adequate nutrition through enteral means."}{"title": "RITMO INICIAL:El ritmo inicial se refiere a la cantidad de nutrici\u00f3n enteral que se administra al comienzo del tratamiento, ajust\u00e1ndose seg\u00fan la edad y el estado del paciente."}{"title": "AUMENTO DIARIO:El aumento diario es la cantidad de nutrici\u00f3n que se incrementa cada d\u00eda en el tratamiento de nutrici\u00f3n enteral, basado en la tolerancia del paciente."}{"title": "M\u00c1XIMO:El m\u00e1ximo se refiere al volumen m\u00e1ximo de nutrici\u00f3n enteral que se puede administrar a un paciente en un d\u00eda, dependiendo de su edad y condici\u00f3n."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N POSTPIL\u00d3RICA:La nutrici\u00f3n postpil\u00f3rica es un tipo de nutrici\u00f3n enteral que se administra m\u00e1s all\u00e1 del p\u00edloro, utilizada en pacientes con ciertas condiciones m\u00e9dicas."}{"title": "PSIC\u00d3LOGO:El psic\u00f3logo es un profesional que apoya el desarrollo emocional y conductual de los ni\u00f1os, especialmente en el contexto de la alimentaci\u00f3n y la nutrici\u00f3n."}{"title": "PEDIATRA:El pediatra es un m\u00e9dico especializado en el cuidado de la salud infantil, que supervisa y prescribe tratamientos para la nutrici\u00f3n enteral en ni\u00f1os."}{"title": "GAUDERER MW:Gauderer MW is an author who has contributed to the field of enteral nutrition, particularly in the context of pediatric care."}{"title": "BAKER SS:Baker SS is an editor and author in pediatric nutrition support literature."}{"title": "RIBE KONINCKX C:Ribe Koninckx C is a coordinator of a publication on pediatric gastroenterology, hepatology, and nutrition."}{"title": "WALKER WA:Walker WA is an editor of the book 'Pediatric Gastrointestinal Disease' which includes discussions on enteral nutrition."}{"title": "DURIE PR:Durie PR is an editor of the book 'Pediatric Gastrointestinal Disease' which covers enteral nutrition topics."}{"title": "HAMILTON JR:Hamilton JR is an editor of the book 'Pediatric Gastrointestinal Disease' which addresses enteral nutrition."}{"title": "WALKER-SMITH JA:Walker-Smith JA is an editor of the book 'Pediatric Gastrointestinal Disease' which includes information on enteral nutrition."}{"title": "WATKINS JB:Watkins JB is an editor of the book 'Pediatric Gastrointestinal Disease' which discusses enteral nutrition."}{"title": "BC DECKER:BC Decker is a publishing company that published the book 'Pediatric Gastrointestinal Disease' which includes enteral nutrition topics."}{"title": "JONES AND BARTLETT PUBLISHERS:Jones and Bartlett Publishers is a publishing company that published works on pediatric nutrition support."}{"title": "MARTA GERM\u00c1N D\u00cdAZ:Marta Germ\u00e1n D\u00edaz is an attending physician in the Pediatrics Service at Hospital Universitario 12 de Octubre."}{"title": "JOS\u00c9 MANUEL MORENO VILLARES:Jos\u00e9 Manuel Moreno Villares is an attending physician in the Clinical Nutrition Unit at Hospital 12 de Octubre."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL EN EL PACIENTE PEDI\u00c1TRICO:A topic discussing the administration of parenteral nutrition specifically for pediatric patients."}{"title": "ATRESIA ILEAL:Ileal atresia is a congenital condition that can cause short bowel syndrome in infants, requiring nutritional intervention."}{"title": "SOLUCIONES NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional solutions are specially formulated mixtures used in parenteral nutrition to meet the dietary needs of patients."}{"title": "EQUIPOS DE SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL:Nutritional support teams are specialized groups responsible for monitoring and managing the nutritional needs of patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DIGESTIVA:Las enfermedades digestivas son condiciones que pueden requerir nutrici\u00f3n parenteral, como la malabsorci\u00f3n intestinal o la necesidad de reposo del tubo digestivo."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD EXTRADIGESTIVA:Las enfermedades extradigestivas son condiciones no relacionadas con el sistema digestivo que tambi\u00e9n pueden requerir nutrici\u00f3n parenteral, como insuficiencia hep\u00e1tica o renal grave."}{"title": "NECESIDADES DE LIQUIDOS:Las necesidades de l\u00edquidos son un componente cr\u00edtico de los requerimientos nutricionales que var\u00edan seg\u00fan la edad, tama\u00f1o corporal y estado de salud del paciente pedi\u00e1trico."}{"title": "HOLLIDAY-SEGAR:El m\u00e9todo de Holliday-Segar es una f\u00f3rmula utilizada para calcular las necesidades h\u00eddricas de mantenimiento en pacientes pedi\u00e1tricos."}{"title": "TERMOG\u00c9NESIS INDUCIDA POR LA DIETA:La termog\u00e9nesis inducida por la dieta es el gasto energ\u00e9tico asociado con la digesti\u00f3n y absorci\u00f3n de nutrientes."}{"title": "GASTO POR ACTIVIDAD F\u00cdSICA:El gasto por actividad f\u00edsica es la energ\u00eda utilizada durante la actividad f\u00edsica, que se calcula mediante un factor de correcci\u00f3n aplicado al gasto energ\u00e9tico basal."}{"title": "GASTO POR CRECIMIENTO:El gasto por crecimiento es el requerimiento energ\u00e9tico adicional necesario para el crecimiento en ni\u00f1os, especialmente durante per\u00edodos de crecimiento acelerado."}{"title": "REQUIERIMIENTOS NUTRICIONALES:"}{"title": "P\u00daRPURA REUMATOIDE SEVERA:P\u00farpura reumatoide severa is a severe autoimmune condition characterized by inflammation and bleeding under the skin, requiring careful management."}{"title": "OXIGENACI\u00d3N CON MEMBRANA EXTRACORP\u00d3REA:Oxigenaci\u00f3n con membrana extracorp\u00f3rea is a medical procedure used to provide oxygen to the blood when the lungs are unable to do so."}{"title": "PERIOPERATORIO:Perioperatorio refers to the period surrounding a surgical procedure, which includes preoperative and postoperative care."}{"title": "QUEMADOS CR\u00cdTICOS:Quemados cr\u00edticos refers to patients with severe burns who require specialized medical care and rehabilitation."}{"title": "FRACASO MULTIORG\u00c1NICO:Fracaso multiorg\u00e1nico is a critical condition where multiple organ systems fail, often requiring intensive care."}{"title": "CAQUEXIA CARD\u00cdACA:Caquexia cardiaca is a syndrome characterized by severe weight loss and muscle wasting due to heart disease."}{"title": "INESTABILIDAD HEMODIN\u00c1MICA:Inestabilidad hemodin\u00e1mica refers to unstable blood circulation, often seen in critically ill patients."}{"title": "MUCOSITIS INTENSA:Mucositis intensa is a severe form of mucositis that can occur in cancer patients undergoing chemotherapy, leading to significant discomfort."}{"title": "TROMBOPENIA GRAVE:Trombopenia grave is a serious condition characterized by a dangerously low platelet count, which can complicate medical treatments."}{"title": "CALOR\u00cdMETR\u00cdA INDIRECTA:A method used to estimate energy expenditure in patients, particularly useful in calculating energy needs for parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "REQUERIMIENTOS DE PROTE\u00cdNA:The specific protein needs that must be calculated first in the context of nutritional support to ensure adequate nitrogen retention."}{"title": "CALOR\u00cdAS NO PROTEICAS:Calories that are not derived from protein, which must be balanced in the nutritional support of patients."}{"title": "FRACASO INTESTINAL:A medical condition that may necessitate the use of parenteral nutrition to provide adequate nutrition to patients."}{"title": "ENERG\u00cdA TOTAL DIARIA:"}{"title": "DIURESIS OSM\u00d3TICA:Diuresis osm\u00f3tica is a condition that can result from excessive glucose administration, leading to increased urine output and potential complications in patients."}{"title": "CO2:CO2, or carbon dioxide, is a byproduct of metabolism that can increase with excessive glucose intake, affecting respiratory function."}{"title": "INTRALIPID:INTRALIPID is a lipid solution that was first marketed in the 1960s. It is composed of long-chain triglycerides derived from soybean oil and contains essential omega-3 and omega-6 fatty acids."}{"title": "OMEGAVEN:Omegaven is a lipid solution made exclusively from fish oil, designed to effectively treat specific conditions in pediatric patients. It is particularly beneficial for individuals suffering from liver disease related to parenteral nutrition, with a notable efficacy in those affected by short bowel syndrome."}{"title": "RECI\u00c9N NACIDO PRET\u00c9RMINO:\"Reci\u00e9n nacido pret\u00e9rmino\" refers to preterm newborns, which are infants born before 37 weeks of gestation. These infants often require specialized nutritional support and specific nutritional guidelines to ensure their health and development."}{"title": "RECI\u00c9N NACIDO A T\u00c9RMINO:Reci\u00e9n nacido a t\u00e9rmino refers to infants born between the 37th and 42nd week of pregnancy, with distinct nutritional needs."}{"title": "PRIMENE\u00ae:Primene\u00ae es otra soluci\u00f3n de amino\u00e1cidos pedi\u00e1tricos dise\u00f1ada para satisfacer las necesidades nutricionales de los ni\u00f1os."}{"title": "AMINOPLASMAL PAED\u00ae:Aminoplasmal Paed\u00ae es una f\u00f3rmula de amino\u00e1cidos pedi\u00e1tricos que proporciona nutrientes esenciales para el crecimiento y desarrollo de los ni\u00f1os."}{"title": "L-ISOLEUCINA:L-Isoleucina es un amino\u00e1cido esencial que se encuentra en las soluciones de amino\u00e1cidos pedi\u00e1tricos y es importante para la s\u00edntesis de prote\u00ednas."}{"title": "L-LEUCINA:L-Leucina es un amino\u00e1cido esencial que juega un papel crucial en la regulaci\u00f3n del crecimiento y la recuperaci\u00f3n muscular."}{"title": "L-LISINA:L-Lisina es un amino\u00e1cido esencial que es fundamental para el crecimiento y la producci\u00f3n de hormonas y enzimas."}{"title": "L-FENILALANINA:L-Fenilalanina es un amino\u00e1cido esencial que se convierte en tirosina y es importante para la producci\u00f3n de neurotransmisores."}{"title": "L-TREONINA:L-Treonina es un amino\u00e1cido esencial que es importante para la formaci\u00f3n de col\u00e1geno y elastina."}{"title": "L-TRIPT\u00d3FANO:L-Tript\u00f3fano es un amino\u00e1cido esencial que se convierte en serotonina, un neurotransmisor que regula el estado de \u00e1nimo."}{"title": "L-VALINA:L-Valina es un amino\u00e1cido esencial que es importante para la energ\u00eda y la recuperaci\u00f3n muscular."}{"title": "L-HISTIDINA:L-Histidina es un amino\u00e1cido esencial que es importante para la producci\u00f3n de histamina y la regulaci\u00f3n del pH."}{"title": "L-CISTE\u00cdNA:L-Ciste\u00edna es un amino\u00e1cido no esencial que posee propiedades antioxidantes y es fundamental para la salud celular."}{"title": "L-ALANINA:L-Alanina is a non-essential amino acid that plays a significant role in glucose metabolism and energy production. It is recognized in both scientific and nutritional contexts for its involvement in these vital processes."}{"title": "SELECIO:El selenio es un oligoelemento que debe ser limitado en pacientes con insuficiencia renal en la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral pedi\u00e1trica."}{"title": "ACCESOS VASCULARES:Accesos vasculares refers to the methods of gaining access to the vascular system for medical treatment, particularly in pediatric nutrition."}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TERES VENOSOS CENTRALES:Cat\u00e9teres venosos centrales are medical devices used for long-term intravenous access, particularly in patients requiring nutritional support."}{"title": "L-ARGININA:L-Arginina is an amino acid that is important for protein synthesis and is mentioned in nutritional recommendations."}{"title": "L-PROLINA:L-Prolina is an amino acid that is significant for collagen production and is included in nutritional discussions."}{"title": "L-SERINA:L-Serina is an amino acid that is involved in various metabolic processes and is referenced in nutritional contexts."}{"title": "GLICINA:Glicina is an amino acid that plays a role in the synthesis of proteins and is mentioned in nutritional recommendations."}{"title": "L-ASPARTICO:L-Aspartico is an amino acid that is important for the synthesis of other amino acids and is included in nutritional discussions."}{"title": "L-GLUT\u00c1MICO:L-Glut\u00e1mico is an amino acid that is crucial for neurotransmission and is referenced in nutritional contexts."}{"title": "L-ORNITINA:L-Ornitina is an amino acid that is involved in the urea cycle and is referenced in nutritional contexts."}{"title": "L-ASPARRIGINA:L-Asparrigina is an amino acid that is important for protein synthesis and is included in nutritional discussions."}{"title": "TABLA 9:Tabla que muestra los aportes de oligoelementos en nutrici\u00f3n parenteral seg\u00fan la edad de los pacientes pedi\u00e1tricos."}{"title": "FE:El hierro es un oligoelemento esencial que se debe proporcionar en nutrici\u00f3n parenteral para prevenir la anemia en pacientes pedi\u00e1tricos."}{"title": "ZN:El zinc es un oligoelemento que es vital para el crecimiento y desarrollo, y debe ser incluido en la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "SE:El selenio es un oligoelemento que act\u00faa como antioxidante y es importante en la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "CR:El cromo es un oligoelemento que puede ser necesario en la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral para el metabolismo de la glucosa."}{"title": "MN:El manganeso es un oligoelemento que se debe incluir en la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral para el metabolismo y la formaci\u00f3n de huesos."}{"title": "MO:El molibdeno es un oligoelemento que se requiere en peque\u00f1as cantidades y debe ser administrado en nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "I:El yodo es un oligoelemento esencial para la funci\u00f3n tiroidea y debe ser considerado en la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "SOLUCIONES TERNARIAS:Ternary solutions in parenteral nutrition consist of amino acids, glucose, and lipids, and are preferred for their comprehensive nutrient delivery."}{"title": "SOLUCIONES BINARIAS:Binary solutions in parenteral nutrition consist of two components, typically amino acids and glucose, administered separately from lipids."}{"title": "BOMBAS DE INFUSI\u00d3N:Infusion pumps are devices used to deliver parenteral nutrition solutions continuously or cyclically to patients."}{"title": "PVC:PVC (polivinyl chloride) is a material used in infusion systems for parenteral nutrition, which should not contain harmful additives like DEHP."}{"title": "DEHP:DEHP (di(2-etilhexil) ftalato) is a plasticizer that should be avoided in materials used for parenteral nutrition due to health concerns."}{"title": "FILTRACI\u00d3N:Filtration is a process used in parenteral nutrition systems to prevent air entry and retain particles and bacteria."}{"title": "SOLUCIONES SIN L\u00cdPIDOS:Solutions without lipids are specific formulations in parenteral nutrition that require different filtration methods."}{"title": "MEZCLAS TERNARIAS:Ternary mixtures in parenteral nutrition refer to the combination of amino acids, glucose, and lipids in a single solution."}{"title": "ETILENO ACETATO DE VINILO:"}{"title": "STAPHYLOCOCCUS EPIDERMIDIS:Staphylococcus epidermidis is a type of bacteria commonly implicated in catheter-related infections."}{"title": "ENTEROBACTER SPP:Enterobacter spp. are bacteria that can cause infections associated with catheters."}{"title": "PSEUDOMONA AERUGINOSA:Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a gram-negative bacterium known for its ability to cause serious infections, particularly in patients with compromised immune systems, such as those with catheters. This opportunistic pathogen poses a significant risk in clinical settings, where it can lead to severe health complications in vulnerable individuals."}{"title": "UROQUINASA:Urokinase is a fibrinolytic agent used to treat occlusions in catheters."}{"title": "LACERACI\u00d3N DE UN VASO:Laceration of a vessel refers to the tearing of a blood vessel, which can occur as a complication during catheter insertion."}{"title": "PERFORACI\u00d3N CARD\u00cdACA:Cardiac perforation is a serious complication that can occur during catheter insertion, leading to cardiac tamponade."}{"title": "EMBOLISMO A\u00c9REO:Air embolism is a condition where air enters the vascular system, which can occur as a complication during catheter insertion."}{"title": "LESI\u00d3N DE UN PLEXO NERVIOSO:Nerve plexus injury refers to damage to a network of nerves, which can occur as a complication during catheter insertion."}{"title": "LOCALIZACI\u00d3N AN\u00d3MALA DEL CAT\u00c9TER:Abnormal catheter placement refers to incorrect positioning of the catheter, which can lead to complications."}{"title": "OCULSI\u00d3N/TROMBOSIS:Occlusion/thrombosis related to the catheter refers to blockage of the catheter, which can limit its function and is a common complication."}{"title": "BAJA CONCENTRACI\u00d3N DE HEPARINA:Low concentration heparin is used in the management of catheter-related complications, particularly to prevent occlusion."}{"title": "FIBRINOL\u00cdTICO:Fibrinolytics are medications used to dissolve blood clots, which can be necessary in the treatment of catheter occlusions."}{"title": "BACTERIEMIAS:Bacteremia refers to the presence of bacteria in the bloodstream, which can occur as a complication of catheter use."}{"title": "PUERTAS DE INFECCI\u00d3N:Infection entry points refer to locations where bacteria can enter the body, particularly relevant in catheter use."}{"title": "PUNTO DE INSERCI\u00d3N:The insertion point is the location on the skin where the catheter is placed, which can be a site for infection."}{"title": "CABEZA DEL CAT\u00c9TER:The catheter tip is the end of the catheter that is placed in the body, which can also be a site for infection.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "ALCOHOL AL 70%:70% alcohol is used as a disinfectant in medical settings to maintain aseptic technique in catheter management."}{"title": "BACTEREMIA:Bacteremia is the presence of bacteria in the blood, often associated with infections related to catheters."}{"title": "CVC TUNELIZADO:Tunneled CVCs are a type of central venous catheter that is inserted under the skin to provide long-term access for treatments."}{"title": "DEFICIT DE VITAMINAS:Vitamin deficiencies can occur in patients receiving parenteral nutrition if not properly supplemented."}{"title": "FRACTURA INTESTINAL:Intestinal failure can lead to complications in patients requiring long-term parenteral nutrition, affecting nutrient absorption."}{"title": "ACIDO URSODEOXIC\u00d3LICO:A medication used to treat liver complications associated with parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITALIZACIONES REPETIDAS:Frequent hospital admissions that can affect the management and outcomes of patients on parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES HEP\u00c1TICAS:Liver complications that can arise from prolonged parenteral nutrition, necessitating careful monitoring and management."}{"title": "PEDIATRIC NUTRITION:The field of nutrition focused on the dietary needs and nutritional support of infants and children."}{"title": "VINARS E:Vinars E is an author who contributed to the history of parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "DUDRICK SJ:Dudrick SJ is an author known for early developments and clinical applications of total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "WILMORE DW:Wilmore DW is an author who has written about the growth and development of infants receiving all nutrients via a vein."}{"title": "MORGAN VILLARES JM:Moreno Villares JM is an author who has written about artificial nutrition in pediatric patients."}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF PEDIATRIC GASTROENTEROLOGY:A professional organization that provides guidelines on pediatric parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "SPANISH SOCIETY OF PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:An organization that focuses on the development and consensus of parenteral nutrition practices in Spain."}{"title": "AGENCY FOR HEALTHCARE RESEARCH AND QUALITY:The Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality (AHRQ) is an organization dedicated to providing evidence-based information on healthcare outcomes, which includes a focus on nutritional support practices. AHRQ has played a significant role in developing guidelines for the American Society of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ASPEN) as well as the European Society of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ESPEN), thereby contributing to the advancement of standards in nutritional care within healthcare settings."}{"title": "NUTRITION IN PEDIATRICS:A comprehensive field that addresses the nutritional needs and interventions for pediatric patients."}{"title": "SU\u00c1REZ L:Su\u00e1rez L is the editor of the practical manual on pediatric nutrition published in Madrid by Ergon in 2007."}{"title": "MORA\u00cdS L\u00d3PEZ A:Mor\u00e1is L\u00f3pez A is an author of practical advice for the prescription of pediatric parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LAMA MORE RA:Lama More RA is a co-author of the practical advice for pediatric parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "GALERA MART\u00cdNEZ R:Galera Mart\u00ednez R is a co-author of the practical advice for pediatric parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "ACTA PEDIATR ESP:Acta Pediatr Esp is the journal where the practical advice for pediatric parenteral nutrition was published."}{"title": "MEHTA NM:Mehta NM is an author who studied energy imbalance and the risk of overfeeding in critically ill children."}{"title": "PEDIATR CRIT CARE MED:Pediatr Crit Care Med is the journal where the study on energy imbalance in critically ill children was published."}{"title": "SCHOFIELD W:Schofield W is an author who contributed to predicting basal metabolic rate and reviewing previous work."}{"title": "HUM NUTR CLIN NUTR:Hum Nutr Clin Nutr is the journal where Schofield's work on basal metabolic rate was published."}{"title": "KRENITSKY J:Krenitsky J is an author who provided evidence supporting the use of adjusted body weight in calculating calorie requirements."}{"title": "MARTINEZ EE:Martinez EE is an author who discussed challenges to nutrition therapy in the pediatric critically ill obese patient."}{"title": "LACAILLE F:Lacaille F is an author who contributed to a position paper on intestinal failure-associated liver disease."}{"title": "KLEIN GW:Klein GW is an author who studied hyperglycemia and its outcomes in the pediatric intensive care unit."}{"title": "PREISSIG CM:Preissig CM is an author who researched pediatric critical illness hyperglycemia."}{"title": "GUANDALINI S:Guandalini S is an editor of a textbook on pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition. This role highlights Guandalini S's expertise and contributions to the field, focusing on the specialized topics of pediatric health, particularly concerning gastrointestinal issues and nutritional needs in children."}{"title": "HOJSAK I:Hojsak I is an author who contributed to a systematic review on intravenous lipid emulsions and hepatotoxicity."}{"title": "COWAN E:Cowan E is an author who studied fish oil-based lipid emulsion in treating parenteral nutrition-associated liver disease."}{"title": "MATSUMOTO CS:Matsumoto CS is an author who researched hepatic explant pathology in pediatric intestinal transplant recipients."}{"title": "MERCER DF:Mercer DF is an author who studied hepatic fibrosis in children treated with intravenous fish oil emulsion."}{"title": "POINDEXTER BB:Poindexter BB is an author who contributed to a textbook on neonatal perinatal medicine."}{"title": "UTHAYA S:Uthaya S is a researcher and author specializing in preterm parenteral nutrition. He has contributed significantly to the field through multiple publications and has conducted reviews on practical aspects of preterm parenteral nutrition. His work reflects a deep engagement with the complexities and challenges associated with providing nutritional support to preterm infants."}{"title": "J PEDIATR:"}{"title": "CURRENT OPIN CLIN NUTR METAB CARE:"}{"title": "CURRENT OPIN PEDIATR:"}{"title": "FARANOFF AND MARTIN'S NEONATAL PERINATAL MEDICINE:"}{"title": "EARLY HUM DEV:"}{"title": "FISH OIL-BASED LIPID EMULSION:Fish oil-based lipid emulsion is a treatment option for parenteral nutrition-associated liver disease in pediatric patients."}{"title": "HYPERGLYCEMIA IN PEDIATRIC INTENSIVE CARE:Hyperglycemia in pediatric intensive care is a critical area of research focusing on its risk factors and outcomes."}{"title": "ELSEVIER SAUNDERS:Elsevier Saunders is a publishing company known for its medical and scientific literature, including textbooks and journals."}{"title": "MODI N:Modi N is a co-author with Uthaya S on research regarding preterm parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LIU X:Liu X is a researcher who contributed to studies on nutritional evaluation in neonates."}{"title": "BABALIS D:Babalis D is a researcher involved in clinical trials related to amino acid regimens in preterm infants."}{"title": "DOR\u00c9 CJ:Dor\u00e9 CJ is a researcher who has co-authored studies on nutrition in preterm infants."}{"title": "WARWICK J:Warwick J is a researcher contributing to the field of pediatric nutrition."}{"title": "BELL J:Bell J is a researcher involved in studies on neonatal nutrition."}{"title": "TRIVEDI A:Trivedi A is a researcher who has published work on the administration of amino acids in preterm infants."}{"title": "SINN JK:Sinn JK is a co-author with Trivedi A on research comparing early and late amino acid administration."}{"title": "VLAARDINGERBROEK H:Vlaardingerbroek H is a researcher studying albumin synthesis in very low birth weight infants."}{"title": "SCHIERBEEK H:Schierbeek H is a researcher involved in studies on nutrition in preterm infants."}{"title": "ROOK D:Rook D is a researcher contributing to the understanding of neonatal nutrition."}{"title": "VERMEULEN MJ:Vermeulen MJ is a researcher studying the effects of nutrition on preterm infants."}{"title": "DORST K:Dorst K is a researcher involved in pediatric nutrition studies."}{"title": "VERMES A:Vermes A is a researcher studying nutrition in very low birth weight infants."}{"title": "BOUBRED F:Boubred F is a researcher focused on the health risks of extremely preterm infants."}{"title": "HERLENIUS E:Herlenius E is a researcher studying the health outcomes of preterm infants."}{"title": "BARTOCCI M:Bartocci M is a researcher involved in studies on preterm infant health."}{"title": "JONSSON B:Jonsson B is a researcher studying the nutritional needs of preterm infants."}{"title": "VANP\u00c9E M:Vanp\u00e9e M is a researcher focused on the health of preterm infants."}{"title": "WATSON RR:Watson RR is an editor involved in the publication of nutrition literature."}{"title": "GRIMBLE G:Grimble G is an editor contributing to the field of nutrition."}{"title": "PREEDY VR:Preedy VR is an editor involved in nutrition research."}{"title": "ZIBADI S:Zibadi S is an editor contributing to literature on nutrition in infancy."}{"title": "JPEN J:JPEN J is a journal focused on parenteral and enteral nutrition."}{"title": "NCP:NCP is a journal that publishes research on nutrition care processes."}{"title": "ACTA PAEDIATR:Acta Paediatr is a journal that publishes research on pediatric health and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITALIZED PEDIATRIC PATIENTS:Hospitalized pediatric patients are children receiving medical care in a hospital setting, often requiring specialized nutrition support."}{"title": "NUT(\"ENTITY\":"}{"title": "NUTRITION IN INFANCY:"}{"title": "PARENTERAL NUTRITION IN INFANTS:Parenteral nutrition in infants is a medical treatment providing nutrition directly into the bloodstream for those unable to eat by mouth."}{"title": "AMINO ACID REGIMEN:Amino acid regimen refers to the specific formulation of amino acids provided to infants, particularly in parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "INTRAVENOUS LIPID EMULSIONS:Intravenous lipid emulsions are fat-based solutions administered to provide essential fatty acids and calories to patients, including preterm infants."}{"title": "AL JG:Al JG is an author who contributed to the study of peripherally inserted central catheters for long-term parenteral nutrition in infants with intestinal failure."}{"title": "AVITZUR Y:Avitzur Y is an author involved in research on peripherally inserted central catheters for infants."}{"title": "WALES PW:Wales PW is an author who co-authored a study on long-term parenteral nutrition in infants."}{"title": "HOSPITAL PHARMACIES:Hospital pharmacies in Switzerland, France, and Belgium are involved in parenteral nutrition practices."}{"title": "AMERICAN SOCIETY OF HOSPITAL PHARMACISTS:The American Society of Hospital Pharmacists published the Handbook of injectable drugs."}{"title": "MOTCHNICK PA:Motchnick PA is an author involved in the study of toxic hydroperoxides in intravenous lipid emulsions."}{"title": "AMES BN:Ames BN is an author who contributed to the research on toxic hydroperoxides in intravenous lipid emulsions."}{"title": "BLACKMER AB:Blackmer AB is an author who wrote about the risks and benefits of three-in-one parenteral nutrition in neonates and pediatric patients."}{"title": "PARTIPILO ML:Partipilo ML is an author who co-authored a study on three-in-one parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "MAISONNEUVE N:Maisonneuve N is an author who researched parenteral nutrition practices in hospital pharmacies."}{"title": "RAGUSO CA:Raguso CA is an author involved in the study of parenteral nutrition practices in hospital pharmacies."}{"title": "PAOLINI-GIACOBINO A:Paolini-Giacobino A is an author who contributed to the research on parenteral nutrition practices."}{"title": "SINGH A:Singh A is an author who wrote about commercial premixed parenteral nutrition in pediatrics."}{"title": "RAUCH D:Rauch D is an author who co-authored a study on commercial premixed parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "HWANG TL:Hwang TL is an author who researched the early use of cyclic TPN in pediatric patients."}{"title": "LUE MC:Lue MC is an author involved in the study of cyclic TPN and liver function in pediatric patients."}{"title": "CHEN LL:Chen LL is an author who contributed to the research on cyclic TPN and liver function."}{"title": "TRISECHMANN U:Trieschmann U is an author who wrote about central venous catheters in children and neonates."}{"title": "TEN F CATE U:Ten F Cate U is an author involved in the study of central venous catheters in children."}{"title": "SREERAM N:Sreeram N is an author who contributed to the research on central venous catheters."}{"title": "MURPHY PC:Murphy PC is an author who researched ultrasound-assisted vascular access in children."}{"title": "ARNOLD P:Arnold P is an author who co-authored a study on ultrasound-assisted vascular access."}{"title": "JOURNEYCAKE JM:Journeycake JM is an author who wrote about thrombotic complications of central venous catheters in children."}{"title": "BUCHANAN GR:Buchanan GR is an author involved in the study of thrombotic complications in pediatric patients."}{"title": "GOOSSENS GA:Goossens GA is an author who researched flushing and locking of venous catheters."}{"title": "VIDAL E:Vidal E is an author who conducted a systematic review on central venous catheter-related thrombosis in children."}{"title": "SHARATHKUMAR A:Sharathkumar A is an author involved in the study of thrombosis related to central venous catheters."}{"title": "GLOVER J:Glover J is an author who contributed to research on central venous catheter-related thrombosis."}{"title": "FAUSTINO EV:Faustino EV is an author who co-authored a systematic review on thrombosis in children."}{"title": "BRAND\u00c3O LR:Brand\u00e3o LR is an author who researched low molecular weight heparin for preventing catheter-related thrombosis in children."}{"title": "SHAH N:Shah N is an author involved in the study of low molecular weight heparin in pediatric patients."}{"title": "SHAH PS:Shah PS is an author who contributed to research on preventing catheter-related thrombosis in children."}{"title": "KERNER JA:Kerner JA is an author who wrote about the treatment of catheter occlusion in pediatric patients."}{"title": "GARCIA-CAREAGA MG:Garcia-Careaga MG is an author involved in the study of catheter occlusion treatment."}{"title": "FISHER AA:Fisher AA is an author who contributed to research on catheter occlusion in pediatric patients."}{"title": "POOLE RL:Poole RL is an author who co-authored a study on catheter occlusion treatment."}{"title": "ALLON M:Allon M is an author involved in the clinical practice guidelines for catheter-related infections."}{"title": "BOUZA E:Bouza E is an author who co-authored guidelines for managing catheter-related infections."}{"title": "CRAVEN DE:Craven DE is an author who contributed to the clinical practice guidelines for catheter-related infections."}{"title": "FLYNN P:Flynn P is an author involved in the clinical practice guidelines for catheter-related infections."}{"title": "O'GRADY NP:O'Grady NP is an author who contributed to the clinical practice guidelines for catheter-related infections."}{"title": "JANUM S:Janum S is an author engaged in research focused on central catheter-related bloodstream infections in children. This work includes addressing the challenges associated with diagnosing these infections, highlighting the complexities and difficulties faced in clinical settings. Through their research and writings, Janum S contributes valuable insights into the understanding and management of these serious health issues affecting pediatric patients."}{"title": "ZINGG W:Zingg W is an author who contributes to the study of catheter-related bloodstream infections, with a specific focus on central catheter-related bloodstream infections in children."}{"title": "CLASSEN V:Classen V is an author recognized for significant contributions to the field of medical research, particularly focusing on catheter-related bloodstream infections. In addition to this, Classen V has also explored the challenges associated with the diagnosis and care of bloodstream infections in children, highlighting the complexities and nuances involved in pediatric healthcare."}{"title": "AFSHARI A:Afshari A is an author recognized for co-authoring a review focused on catheter-related bloodstream infections. This review specifically addresses central catheter-related bloodstream infections in children, highlighting Afshari A's contributions to this important area of medical research."}{"title": "GERM\u00c1N D\u00cdAZ M:Germ\u00e1n D\u00edaz M is an author who has researched antibiotic and antiseptic sealing in pediatric patients with home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LE\u00d3N SANZ M:Le\u00f3n Sanz M is an author who has researched sealing methods in pediatric patients with home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "WONG T:Wong T is an author who has studied central venous catheter thrombosis in pediatric patients on home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CLIFFORD V:Clifford V is an author contributing to the research on catheter thrombosis in pediatric patients."}{"title": "MCCALLUM Z:McCallum Z is an author involved in the case series on central venous catheter thrombosis."}{"title": "BISSELING TM:Bisseling TM is an author who has researched the effectiveness of taurolidine lock in preventing infections in patients on home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "WILLEMS MC:Willems MC is an author contributing to the study of taurolidine lock in preventing infections."}{"title": "VERSLEIJEN MW:Versleijen MW is an author involved in the prospective trial on taurolidine lock effectiveness."}{"title": "HOWARD L:Howard L is an author who has researched the management of complications in patients receiving home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "ASHLEY C:Ashley C is an author contributing to the management of complications in home parenteral nutrition patients."}{"title": "BYRNES MC:Byrnes MC is an author who has studied refeeding in the ICU for both adults and pediatric patients."}{"title": "STANGENES J:Stangenes J is an author involved in the research on refeeding problems in the ICU."}{"title": "CROOK MA:Crook MA is an author who has researched the importance of refeeding syndrome."}{"title": "HALLY V:Hally V is an author contributing to the study of refeeding syndrome."}{"title": "PANTELLI JV:Pantelli JV is an author involved in the research on refeeding syndrome."}{"title": "DEMEHRI FR:Demehri FR is an author who has studied predictors of metabolic bone disease in pediatric intestinal failure."}{"title": "SIMHA S:Simha S is an author contributing to the research on metabolic bone disease in pediatric patients."}{"title": "STEPHENSA L:Stephensa L is an author involved in the study of metabolic bone disease predictors."}{"title": "HARRIS MB:Harris MB is an author who has researched metabolic bone disease in pediatric intestinal failure."}{"title": "ARNOLD MA:Arnold MA is an author contributing to the study of metabolic bone disease in pediatric patients."}{"title": "BROWN PI:Brown PI is an author involved in the research on metabolic bone disease in pediatric intestinal failure."}{"title": "TEITELBAUM DH:Teitelbaum DH is an author who has studied pediatric intestinal failure and its complications."}{"title": "BLANCA GARC\u00cdA JA:Blanca Garc\u00eda JA is an author who has researched liver and bone affections associated with parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "MOR\u00c1IS L\u00d3PEZ AB:Mor\u00e1is L\u00f3pez AB is an author contributing to the study of liver and bone issues in parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CORTES MORA P:Cortes Mora P is an author involved in the research on liver and bone affections in parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LAURITI G:Lauriti G is an author who has studied the incidence and treatment of liver disease in infants and children on parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "ZANI A:Zani A is an author contributing to the research on liver disease associated with parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "AUFIERI R:Aufieri R is an author involved in the study of liver disease in infants and children on parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CANANZI M:Cananzi M is an author who has researched liver disease in pediatric patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CHIESA PL:Chiesa PL is an author contributing to the study of liver disease in children on parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "EATON S:Eaton S is an author involved in the research on liver disease in pediatric patients."}{"title": "PIERRO A:Pierro A is an author who has studied liver disease in infants and children on parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "RANGEL SJ:Rangel SJ is an author who has researched parenteral nutrition-associated cholestasis in pediatric patients."}{"title": "CALKINS CM:Calkins CM is an author contributing to the study of cholestasis in pediatric patients."}{"title": "COWLES RA:Cowles RA is an author involved in the research on cholestasis in pediatric patients."}{"title": "BARNHART DC:Barnhart DC is an author who has studied cholestasis in pediatric patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "HUANG EY:Huang EY is an author contributing to the research on cholestasis in pediatric patients."}{"title": "ABDULLAH F:Abdullah F is an author involved in the study of cholestasis in pediatric patients."}{"title": "BTAICHE IF:Btaiche IF is an author who has researched metabolic complications of parenteral nutrition in adults."}{"title": "KHALIDI N:Khalidi N is an author contributing to the study of metabolic complications in adults receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "PEYRET B:Peyret B is an author who has studied liver complications in children receiving long-term parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "COLLARDEAU S:Collardeau S is an author contributing to the research on liver complications in children."}{"title": "TOUZET S:Touzet S is an author involved in the study of liver complications in pediatric patients."}{"title": "LORAS-DUCLAUX I:Loras-Duclaux I is an author who has researched liver complications in children on parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "YANTRON H:Yantren H is an author contributing to the study of liver complications in children."}{"title": "MICHALSKI MC:Michalski MC is an author involved in the research on liver complications in pediatric patients."}{"title": "FORCHIELLI ML:Forchielli ML is an author who has studied nutritional factors contributing to cholestasis during total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL FACTORS:Nutritional factors are elements that contribute to the development of cholestasis during total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CHOLESTASIS:Cholestasis is a condition that can occur in patients receiving parenteral nutrition, particularly in infants and children."}{"title": "HOME PARENTERAL NUTRITION:Home parenteral nutrition is a medical treatment designed for patients who are unable to obtain sufficient nutrition through oral intake. This therapy involves delivering nutrients directly into the bloodstream, allowing patients to receive essential nutrition intravenously in the comfort of their own homes. It is particularly beneficial for individuals with severe digestive issues, who may require this form of nutritional support to maintain their health and well-being."}{"title": "LONG-TERM PARENTERAL NUTRITION:Long-term parenteral nutrition refers to the extended use of parenteral nutrition in patients, often leading to complications."}{"title": "REVIEW:A review is a comprehensive assessment of existing literature on a particular subject, such as the management of complications in home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CASE SERIES:A case series is a type of research study that tracks patients with a known exposure or treatment, such as central venous catheter thrombosis in pediatric patients."}{"title": "PROSPECTIVE TRIAL:A prospective trial is a research study that follows participants forward in time to evaluate the effects of a treatment, such as taurolidine lock in preventing infections."}{"title": "PEDIATRIC SURGICAL ASSOCIATION:The American Pediatric Surgical Association is an organization focused on improving surgical care for children, including those with intestinal failure."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL HOSPITAL:Nutritional Hospital is a facility that specializes in providing nutritional support and care for patients, particularly those requiring parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO NTRA. SRA. DE CANDELARIA:A hospital located in Tenerife, where Jos\u00e9 Enrique Palacio Abizanda serves as the Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service."}{"title": "JOS\u00c9 ENRIQUE PALACIO ABIZANDA:Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Universitario Ntra. Sra. de Candelaria in Tenerife."}{"title": "DRES. JOS\u00c9 ENRIQUE PALACIO ABIZANDA:A medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, co-authoring topics on ethical and legal aspects of nutritional support."}{"title": "DRES. JULIA \u00c1LVAREZ HERN\u00c1NDEZ:A medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, co-authoring topics on ethical and legal aspects of nutritional support."}{"title": "DRES. ALFONSO VIDAL CASARIEGO:Dres. Alfonso Vidal Casariego is a medical professional who specializes in clinical nutrition management and is also actively involved in nutrition research. His expertise encompasses both the practical application of nutritional strategies in clinical settings and the investigation of nutritional science, contributing to advancements in the field."}{"title": "DRES. DAVID EMILIO BARAJAS GALINDO:A medical professional involved in clinical nutrition management."}{"title": "DRES. ISIDORO CANO RODR\u00cdGUEZ:A medical professional involved in clinical nutrition management."}{"title": "DRAS. MILAGROS P\u00c9REZ RODR\u00cdGUEZ:A medical professional involved in the design and development of clinical nutrition products."}{"title": "DRAS. \u00c1FRICA JIM\u00c9NEZ JIM\u00c9NEZ:A medical professional involved in the design and development of clinical nutrition products."}{"title": "DRES. ALICIA CALLEJA FERN\u00c1NDEZ:A medical professional involved in nutrition research."}{"title": "DRES. BEGO\u00d1A PINTOR DE LA MAZA:A medical professional involved in nutrition research."}{"title": "DRES. MIRIAM ALEJO RAMOS:A medical professional involved in nutrition research."}{"title": "DRA. MAR\u00cdA DOLORES BALLESTEROS POMAR:"}{"title": "DERECHO SANITARIO:Health law encompasses regulations and ethical standards that govern medical practices and patient rights."}{"title": "CONSTITUCI\u00d3N:The Constitution of Spain provides the legal framework for patient rights and healthcare regulations."}{"title": "PARLAMENTO ESPA\u00d1OL:The Spanish Parliament enacts laws that govern healthcare practices and patient rights in Spain."}{"title": "COMUNIDADES AUT\u00d3NOMAS:The \"COMUNIDADES AUT\u00d3NOMAS\" refer to the autonomous communities in Spain, which possess their own regulations and laws concerning healthcare and patient rights. Each autonomous community is responsible for managing health services within its respective jurisdiction, leading to variations in the organization and regulation of healthcare practices. Notably, there are differences in the regulation of home artificial nutrition across these communities, reflecting the diverse approaches to healthcare management within Spain's autonomous regions."}{"title": "HUELGA DE HAMBRE:\"HUELGA DE HAMBRE\" refers to a hunger strike, which is a form of protest where individuals refuse to eat in order to draw attention to their demands or grievances, particularly in detention settings. This method of protest is often undertaken by inmates who seek to highlight their conditions or treatment. While hunger strikes can be a powerful means of advocacy, they also pose significant ethical dilemmas in healthcare, especially concerning patient rights and the implications for medical intervention. Additionally, engaging in a huelga de hambre carries serious risks, including the potential for death or permanent harm to the individuals involved."}{"title": "M\u00c9DICO:M\u00c9DICO refers to a healthcare professional who plays a crucial role in diagnosing and treating patients. This individual is responsible for evaluating the necessity of treatment and may intervene in cases of involuntary hospitalization. Additionally, M\u00c9DICO must navigate various ethical dilemmas in their practice, ensuring that patient care is both effective and ethically sound."}{"title": "VALORES:Values are fundamental beliefs that influence ethical decision-making in healthcare."}{"title": "DIGNIDAD HUMANA:Human dignity is a core principle that underpins ethical considerations in medical practice and patient care."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE CUIDADOS PALIATIVOS:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Cuidados Paliativos (SECPAL) is an organization that addresses issues related to palliative care and ethical decisions at the end of life."}{"title": "CULTURA MEDITERR\u00c1NEA:The Mediterranean culture is characterized by its approach to care and treatment, emphasizing family protection and the importance of hydration and nutrition as symbols of care."}{"title": "CULTURA ANGLOSAXONA:The Anglo-Saxon culture emphasizes individual autonomy and the right to make informed decisions regarding health care, particularly at the end of life."}{"title": "PACIENTES TERMINALES:Terminal patients are those who have exhausted therapeutic options and have a limited life expectancy, often facing ethical and legal dilemmas in their care."}{"title": "DECISION \u00c9TICA:An ethical decision is a choice made regarding the care of individuals, particularly in critical situations such as end-of-life care, which can have irreversible consequences."}{"title": "CUIDADO:CUIDADO refers to the concept of care, which encompasses the actions taken to support and maintain the health and well-being of individuals, particularly in medical contexts. This notion of care extends to providing support for individuals, especially at the end of life, and is viewed variably across different cultures."}{"title": "TERRY SCHIAVO:Terry Schiavo was a woman involved in a highly publicized legal case regarding the withdrawal of life support and enteral nutrition due to her persistent vegetative state."}{"title": "EUGLANA ENGLANO:Euglana Englano is another individual referenced in discussions about the ethical and legal implications of withdrawing enteral nutrition in patients with permanent vegetative states."}{"title": "AUTONOM\u00cdA DEL PACIENTE:AUTONOM\u00cdA DEL PACIENTE refers to the right of patients to make informed decisions regarding their medical care and treatment. This concept emphasizes that patients have the authority to choose their course of action in healthcare matters, including critical aspects such as nutrition and hydration. The principle of patient autonomy underscores the importance of informed consent and the respect for individual preferences in the context of medical decision-making."}{"title": "CONSENTIMIENTO INFORMADO:\"CONSENTIMIENTO INFORMADO\" refers to the process of obtaining voluntary agreement from participants before they engage in clinical trials or medical treatments. It is a fundamental aspect of healthcare that requires patients to provide their free and informed consent after receiving adequate information about the proposed interventions. This process is both a legal and ethical obligation, ensuring that patients are fully aware of and agree to the medical procedures and treatments they will undergo. In summary, \"CONSENTIMIENTO INFORMADO\" is essential for protecting patient autonomy and ensuring informed decision-making in medical contexts."}{"title": "DIRECTIVAS ANTICIPADAS:DIRECTIVAS ANTICIPADAS are legal documents that enable individuals to outline their preferences for medical treatment in situations where they may become unable to communicate their wishes. These documents serve as a means for individuals to express their desires regarding medical care, ensuring that their treatment aligns with their values and choices, even when they cannot voice them."}{"title": "TESTAMENTO VITAL:The \"TESTAMENTO VITAL,\" also known as a living will, is a legal document that serves as an advance directive. It specifies an individual's preferences regarding medical treatment and life-sustaining measures in situations where they are unable to make decisions for themselves. This document outlines the person's wishes concerning their medical care, ensuring that their preferences are respected even when they cannot communicate them directly."}{"title": "BEGO\u00d1A ROM\u00c1N:Bego\u00f1a Rom\u00e1n is a professor at the University of Barcelona, where she contributes to the academic community through her teaching and research. In addition to her academic role, she serves as the President of the Ethics Committee of Social Services in Catalonia, overseeing ethical standards and practices within the social services sector. Furthermore, she is a member of the Bioethics Committee of Catalonia, where she engages in discussions and decisions regarding ethical issues in the field of bioethics."}{"title": "UNIVERSITY OF BARCELONA:The University of Barcelona is a public university in Spain where Bego\u00f1a Rom\u00e1n teaches."}{"title": "CATALONIA:Catalonia is an autonomous community in northeastern Spain, where the Ethics Committee of Social Services operates."}{"title": "ETHICS COMMITTEE OF SOCIAL SERVICES OF CATALONIA:The Ethics Committee of Social Services of Catalonia is responsible for addressing ethical issues in social services in the region."}{"title": "BIOETHICS COMMITTEE OF CATALONIA:The Bioethics Committee of Catalonia provides guidance on ethical issues related to health and medical practices in the region."}{"title": "CONFLICTOS \u00c9TICOS:Conflictos \u00e9ticos refer to ethical dilemmas that arise in medical and healthcare settings, particularly concerning end-of-life decisions and patient autonomy."}{"title": "PRINCIPIO DE PROPORCIONALIDAD:El principio de proporcionalidad is an ethical principle that states that medical treatment should only be provided if the benefits outweigh the burdens for the patient."}{"title": "CUIDADOS B\u00c1SICOS:Cuidados b\u00e1sicos refer to fundamental care practices provided to all individuals, including those who are unable to eat or drink normally."}{"title": "ACUERDOS:Acuerdos refer to agreements made among healthcare professionals, patients, and families regarding treatment decisions, especially in complex cases."}{"title": "MODELOS CULTURALES:Modelos culturales refer to the cultural frameworks that influence healthcare practices and decision-making processes in different societies.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD DE BARCELONA:The University of Barcelona is an educational institution where Bego\u00f1a Rom\u00e1n teaches."}{"title": "DIEGO GRACIA:Diego Gracia is a professor who advocates for a deliberative process in clinical nutrition decision-making."}{"title": "COMIT\u00c9 DE \u00c9TICA DE LOS SERVICIOS SOCIALES DE CATALU\u00d1A:The Ethics Committee of Social Services in Catalonia oversees ethical practices in social services."}{"title": "COMIT\u00c9 DE BIO\u00c9TICA DE CATALU\u00d1A:The Bioethics Committee of Catalonia addresses ethical issues in healthcare and bioethics."}{"title": "LEY GENERAL DE SANIDAD:The General Health Law regulates health rights and services in Spain."}{"title": "CONSTITUCI\u00d3N ESPA\u00d1OLA:The Constituci\u00f3n Espa\u00f1ola is the Spanish Constitution that serves as the foundational legal framework for the country. It delineates the fundamental rights and freedoms of individuals in Spain, ensuring the protection of various rights, including the right to health protection. This constitution plays a crucial role in safeguarding the liberties and well-being of the Spanish populace."}{"title": "PROCESO DELIBERATIVO:The deliberative process involves structured discussions to make ethical decisions in clinical settings."}{"title": "DERECHOS DE LOS PACIENTES:Patient rights are outlined in the General Health Law and are essential for ethical healthcare practices."}{"title": "DECLARACI\u00d3N UNIVERSAL DE DERECHOS HUMANOS:La Declaraci\u00f3n Universal de Derechos Humanos es un documento adoptado por la ONU en 1948 que establece los derechos fundamentales de todas las personas."}{"title": "CONVENIO DEL CONSEJO DE EUROPA PARA LA PROTECCI\u00d3N DE LOS DERECHOS HUMANOS:Este convenio, que entr\u00f3 en vigor en el Reino de Espa\u00f1a el 1 de enero de 2000, establece un marco jur\u00eddico vinculante para la protecci\u00f3n de los derechos humanos en biolog\u00eda y medicina."}{"title": "LEY 41/2002:The Ley 41/2002 is a significant piece of Spanish legislation that was enacted on November 14, 2002. It regulates the autonomy of patients and outlines their rights and obligations concerning information and clinical documentation within the healthcare system in Spain. This law emphasizes the importance of respecting patient autonomy and mandates the necessity of informed consent for medical treatments. Through its provisions, Ley 41/2002 establishes clear guidelines to ensure that patients are adequately informed and can make autonomous decisions regarding their healthcare."}{"title": "PRINCIPIO DE AUTONOM\u00cdA:El principio de autonom\u00eda es un concepto \u00e9tico que sostiene que los individuos tienen el derecho a tomar decisiones sobre su propia vida y cuerpo."}{"title": "PRINCIPIO DE BENEFICENCIA:El principio de beneficencia es un principio \u00e9tico que implica actuar en el mejor inter\u00e9s del paciente y promover su bienestar."}{"title": "DERECHOS HUMANOS:"}{"title": "LEY:La ley establece los derechos de los pacientes en relaci\u00f3n con el consentimiento informado y la informaci\u00f3n que deben recibir antes de cualquier intervenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica."}{"title": "INTERVENCI\u00d3N QUIR\u00daRGICA:La intervenci\u00f3n quir\u00fargica es un procedimiento m\u00e9dico que requiere el consentimiento informado del paciente, especialmente cuando implica riesgos significativos."}{"title": "PROCEDIMIENTOS DIAGN\u00d3STICOS:Los procedimientos diagn\u00f3sticos son intervenciones que pueden requerir el consentimiento informado del paciente, dependiendo de su naturaleza y riesgos."}{"title": "PACIENTE MENOR DE EDAD:El paciente menor de edad es un individuo que no ha alcanzado la mayor\u00eda de edad y puede necesitar consentimiento por representaci\u00f3n para intervenciones m\u00e9dicas."}{"title": "RIESGOS:Los riesgos son las posibles consecuencias negativas que pueden surgir de una intervenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica y que deben ser comunicados al paciente."}{"title": "CONSENTIMIENTO POR REPRESENTACI\u00d3N:El consentimiento por representaci\u00f3n es el proceso mediante el cual se obtiene autorizaci\u00f3n para una intervenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica en nombre de un paciente que no puede tomar decisiones por s\u00ed mismo."}{"title": "REAL DECRETO 124/2007:El Real Decreto 124/2007 regula el Registro Nacional de Instrucciones Previas y el fichero automatizado de datos de car\u00e1cter personal en Espa\u00f1a."}{"title": "REPRESENTANTE LEGAL:El representante legal es una persona designada para actuar en nombre del paciente en cuestiones legales y m\u00e9dicas, especialmente cuando el paciente no puede expresar su voluntad."}{"title": "INSTRUCCIONES PREVIAS:Las instrucciones previas son documentos donde una persona expresa su voluntad sobre tratamientos m\u00e9dicos futuros en caso de que no pueda comunicarse."}{"title": "CONVENIO DE BIO\u00c9TICA DE OVIEDO:El Convenio de Bio\u00e9tica de Oviedo regula la protecci\u00f3n de las personas con trastornos mentales y las condiciones bajo las cuales pueden recibir tratamiento sin su consentimiento."}{"title": "LEY 1/2000:Ley 1/2000 is a Spanish law enacted on January 7, 2000, that regulates involuntary internment due to mental disorders in Spain. Additionally, it pertains to civil procedure within the Spanish legal framework. This law addresses the legal processes and conditions under which individuals may be involuntarily committed for psychiatric reasons, ensuring that such actions are governed by established civil procedures."}{"title": "TRASTORNO MENTAL:Condici\u00f3n que puede llevar a la intervenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica sin consentimiento si se considera que hay un riesgo grave para la salud del paciente."}{"title": "AUTORIDAD JUDICIAL:The \"AUTORIDAD JUDICIAL\" is an entity that plays a crucial role in legal matters concerning the treatment and rights of individuals, particularly in cases where there is a need for authorization for the involuntary internment of a patient. This authority is responsible for ensuring that legal protocols are followed and that the rights of those affected are upheld during such processes."}{"title": "AUDIENCIA PROVINCIAL DE BARCELONA:The Audiencia Provincial de Barcelona is a court that ruled on the case of a young woman with anorexia nerviosa, ordering her involuntary internment due to her mental disorder."}{"title": "BADALONA:Badalona is a city in Spain where the initial ruling regarding the internment of the patient was made."}{"title": "TRIBUNAL:The tribunal is the judicial body that hears cases and makes decisions regarding the internment of individuals, including the patient in this case."}{"title": "SERVICIOS DE ASISTENCIA AL MENOR:The Servicios de Asistencia al Menor are services that provide assistance and support to minors, particularly in legal and health matters."}{"title": "INTERNAMIENTO:Internamiento refers to the involuntary confinement of individuals in a mental health facility, as discussed in the context of the patient's case."}{"title": "FACULTATIVO:A facultativo is a medical professional or doctor who provides care and assessments regarding the health of patients, including those subject to internment."}{"title": "MINISTERIO FISCAL:The Ministerio Fiscal is the public prosecutor's office in Spain, tasked with upholding the law and safeguarding the rights of individuals in legal matters."}{"title": "ORGANIZACI\u00d3N M\u00c9DICA MUNDIAL:La Organizaci\u00f3n M\u00e9dica Mundial es una entidad que establece normas para la atenci\u00f3n de pacientes, incluyendo aquellos en huelga de hambre, y revis\u00f3 su declaraci\u00f3n en Malta en 1991 y en Pilanesberg en 2006."}{"title": "LEY ORG\u00c1NICA 1/1979:The Ley Org\u00e1nica 1/1979, enacted on September 26, 1979, is known as the General Penitentiary Law in Spain. This law establishes regulations concerning the life, integrity, and health of individuals incarcerated in penitentiary institutions. It aims to ensure the humane treatment of inmates and outlines the standards that govern their conditions of confinement."}{"title": "PILANESBERG:Pilanesberg es un lugar donde se revis\u00f3 la declaraci\u00f3n de la Organizaci\u00f3n M\u00e9dica Mundial en 2006."}{"title": "MALTA:Malta es un lugar donde se revis\u00f3 la declaraci\u00f3n de la Organizaci\u00f3n M\u00e9dica Mundial en 1991."}{"title": "INSTITUCIONES SANITARIAS:Las instituciones sanitarias son lugares donde se atienden a personas, incluyendo a aquellos en huelga de hambre."}{"title": "REAL DECRETO 190/1996:The \"REAL DECRETO 190/1996\" is a significant legislative measure in Spain, enacted on February 9, 1996. It approves the Penitentiary Regulations, which are designed to develop and implement the provisions of the Ley Org\u00e1nica 1/1979. This decree establishes the framework for the management and operation of penitentiary institutions in Spain, ensuring that the regulations align with the overarching legal principles set forth in the earlier law."}{"title": "DILEMA \u00c9TICO:El dilema \u00e9tico se refiere a la situaci\u00f3n compleja que enfrentan los m\u00e9dicos al tratar a personas en huelga de hambre, donde se deben equilibrar la beneficencia y el respeto a la autonom\u00eda individual."}{"title": "ADMINISTRACI\u00d3N PENITENCIARIA:The Administraci\u00f3n Penitenciaria is the governmental entity tasked with overseeing the management of prisons. Its primary responsibilities include safeguarding the life, integrity, and health of inmates within penitentiary institutions. This organization plays a crucial role in ensuring that the rights of inmates are upheld while they serve their sentences."}{"title": "CENTRO PENITENCIARIO:El centro penitenciario es un establecimiento donde se encuentran internos y se les proporciona atenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica y otros servicios."}{"title": "ART\u00cdCULO 36:El art\u00edculo 36 de la Ley Org\u00e1nica 1/1979 establece normas sobre la asistencia sanitaria en los centros penitenciarios."}{"title": "ART\u00cdCULO 45:El art\u00edculo 45 de la Ley Org\u00e1nica 1/1979 establece las condiciones bajo las cuales se pueden utilizar medios coercitivos en los internos."}{"title": "PERSONAS EN HUELGA DE HAMBRE:"}{"title": "MADRID-2:Madrid-2 is a preventive prison center where inmates are held and medical treatment is administered in cases of hunger strikes."}{"title": "SORIA:Soria is a location where the Judicial Surveillance Court issued a providence regarding hunger strikes of inmates."}{"title": "GRAPO:GRAPO is a collective of political prisoners in Spain, recognized for their participation in hunger strikes. This group of inmates has raised significant ethical and legal concerns regarding their treatment within the prison system. Their actions highlight the ongoing struggle for improved conditions and rights for prisoners, drawing attention to the broader issues of justice and human rights in the context of incarceration."}{"title": "TRIBUNAL CONSTITUCIONAL:The Tribunal Constitucional, also known as the Constitutional Court of Spain, serves as the highest authority in matters concerning the constitutionality of laws and the protection of fundamental rights within the country. It plays a crucial role in ensuring that both legislative actions and governmental measures adhere to the Spanish Constitution. Notably, the Tribunal has made significant rulings regarding the rights of inmates, including those who engage in hunger strikes, thereby influencing the legal landscape surrounding human rights in Spain. Through its decisions, the Tribunal Constitucional upholds the principles of justice and constitutional governance, reinforcing the rule of law in the nation."}{"title": "LOGP:LOGP refers to the General Penitentiary Law, which outlines the rights and treatment of inmates in Spain."}{"title": "JUZGADO DE VIGILANCIA PENITENCIARIA:The Judicial Surveillance Court oversees the treatment and rights of inmates, ensuring their health and safety."}{"title": "INTERNOS:Internos refers to inmates who are subject to medical treatment and legal oversight, particularly in cases of hunger strikes."}{"title": "CENTRO DIRECTIVO:The Central Directorate is responsible for overseeing the operations and management of penitentiary institutions in Spain."}{"title": "CENTRO PENITENCIARIO DE PREVENTIVOS MADRID-2:"}{"title": "JUZGADO DE VIGILANCIA PENITENCIARIA N\u00ba 2 DE MADRID:The Juzgado de Vigilancia Penitenciaria n\u00ba 2 de Madrid is a court that oversees the treatment and rights of prisoners in Madrid."}{"title": "AUDIENCIA PROVINCIAL DE MADRID:The Audiencia Provincial de Madrid is a provincial court in Madrid that handles appeals and other legal matters."}{"title": "ASISTENCIA M\u00c9DICA:Asistencia m\u00e9dica refers to the medical assistance that is mandated to be provided to prisoners, especially those on hunger strike, to ensure their health and safety."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N FORZOSA:Alimentaci\u00f3n forzosa refers to the forced feeding of prisoners who refuse to eat, which is a contentious legal and ethical issue."}{"title": "SENTENCIA 120/1990:Sentencia 120/1990 is a ruling by the Tribunal Constitucional regarding the limits of medical assistance and fundamental rights of prisoners."}{"title": "LEY Y REGLAMENTO PENITENCIARIO:The Ley y Reglamento penitenciario are the legal frameworks governing the treatment and rights of prisoners in Spain."}{"title": "CONVENIO DE OVIEDO:The Convenio de Oviedo is an international treaty aimed at protecting human rights in the biomedical field."}{"title": "DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH:The Department of Health is a governmental department in the UK responsible for public health and health services."}{"title": "DR. MIKE STROUD:Dr. Mike Stroud is the director of the Department of Nutrition in Southampton, known for his work on clinical management in detention settings."}{"title": "BIO\u00c9TICA:Bio\u00e9tica refers to the study of ethical issues arising from advances in biology and medicine, particularly in healthcare."}{"title": "JURISPRUDENCIA:Jurisprudencia refers to the body of court decisions that interpret laws and can influence future legal cases, including those related to medical ethics and prisoners' rights."}{"title": "HASTING CENTER REPORT:The Hasting Center Report is a publication that discusses ethical issues in medicine and healthcare, including priorities in medical practice."}{"title": "FUNDACI\u00d3 V\u00cdCTOR GR\u00cdFOLS I LUCAS:Fundaci\u00f3 V\u00edctor Gr\u00edfols i Lucas is an organization that publishes works related to medical ethics and bioethics, including the importance of nutrition in clinical settings."}{"title": "SOCIETY OF SPANISH PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:The Society of Spanish Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition is an organization dedicated to enhancing nutritional support in clinical settings. It emphasizes specialized nutritional support and addresses the ethical aspects associated with this field. Through its initiatives, the society aims to improve the quality of care provided to patients requiring parenteral and enteral nutrition."}{"title": "TERRI SCHIAVO:Terri Schiavo was a woman whose case raised significant ethical questions regarding life support and artificial nutrition."}{"title": "ELUANA ENGLARO:Eluana Englaro was a woman whose case involved the withdrawal of artificial nutrition and hydration, sparking ethical debates."}{"title": "J ALVAREZ:J Alvarez is a coordinator involved in the publication of works related to bioethics and clinical nutrition."}{"title": "R BURGOS:R Burgos is a coordinator who contributed to the publication on bioethics in clinical nutrition."}{"title": "S\u00c1NCHEZ-CARO J:S\u00e1nchez-Caro J is an author who has written about ethical and legal implications of nutritional support at the end of life."}{"title": "MERCER DA:Merrell DA is an author who wrote about the ethical implications of life support in the case of Terri Schiavo."}{"title": "GRACIA D:Gracia D is an author who has written about decision-making procedures in clinical ethics."}{"title": "NAVARRO SANZ JR:Navarro Sanz JR is an author discussing palliative care and ethical considerations in terminal illness."}{"title": "AGULLAS SIM\u00d3 P:Agullas Sim\u00f3 P is an author who reviewed the concept of \"living wills\" in the context of medical ethics."}{"title": "MORESCHI C:Moreschi C is an author discussing ethical issues in nutrition support for severely disabled elderly persons."}{"title": "MONOD S:Monod S is an author who has written about ethical issues in nutrition support for elderly patients."}{"title": "LEY 14/1986:Ley 14/1986 is a Spanish law concerning general health that outlines rights and regulations in healthcare."}{"title": "CONVENIO PARA LA PROTECCI\u00d3N DE LOS DERECHOS HUMANOS:The \"CONVENIO PARA LA PROTECCI\u00d3N DE LOS DERECHOS HUMANOS,\" also known as the Convention for the Protection of Human Rights and Dignity of the Human Being with regard to the Applications of Biology and Medicine, is a significant international treaty that emphasizes the dignity of human beings in the context of biological applications. This convention was signed in Oviedo on April 4, 1997, and it aims to safeguard human rights in relation to advancements in biology and medicine."}{"title": "B ROM\u00c1N MAESTRE:"}{"title": "DAVID EMILIO BARAJAS GALINDO:David Emilio Barajas Galindo is an author associated with the field of clinical nutrition and dietetics."}{"title": "ISIDORO CANO RODR\u00cdGUEZ:Isidoro Cano Rodr\u00edguez is an author associated with the field of clinical nutrition and dietetics."}{"title": "COMPLEJO ASISTENCIAL UNIVERSITARIO LE\u00d3N:The Complejo Asistencial Universitario Le\u00f3n, also known as the University Assistance Complex of Le\u00f3n, is a prominent healthcare institution that employs professionals such as Roc\u00edo Villar Taibo, Ana Urioste Fondo, and Paula Fern\u00e1ndez Mart\u00ednez. This institution is actively involved in clinical nutrition and dietetics, providing specialized services in these areas. Additionally, the University Hospital of Le\u00f3n, which is part of this complex, features a Clinical Nutrition Unit dedicated to both research and patient care in nutrition, further emphasizing its commitment to advancing healthcare in this field."}{"title": "SANIDAD:Sanidad refers to the healthcare system in Spain, which is facing challenges due to demographic changes and economic factors."}{"title": "SISTEMA SANITARIO:The healthcare system in Spain, which is challenged by an aging population and rising healthcare costs."}{"title": "IGNACIO JAUREGUI LOBERA:Ignacio Jauregui Lobera is an author who has written about eating disorders and the psychological maturity of minors for decision-making."}{"title": "DECLARACI\u00d3N DE MALTA DE LA AMM:The Malta Declaration by the World Medical Association addresses issues related to individuals on hunger strikes."}{"title": "OFFENDER HEALTH, DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH:The Offender Health department collaborates with medical professionals to provide guidelines for clinical management of individuals refusing food in detention settings."}{"title": "GOBIERNO DE ESPA\u00d1A:The Government of Spain is the national executive body responsible for the administration of the country. It plays a crucial role in establishing health policies and regulations, which encompass areas related to nutrition and healthcare services. As the governing authority, the Government of Spain is tasked with the implementation of laws and the overall management of the nation's affairs."}{"title": "SENADO:The Senate of Spain is the legislative body that approved a motion regarding nutritional strategies in healthcare."}{"title": "PACIENTES SANITARIOS:Patients who are receiving healthcare services and may be affected by nutritional issues."}{"title": "SERVICIOS SOCIOSANITARIOS:Social healthcare services that support patients, particularly those with nutritional needs."}{"title": "GESTI\u00d3N SANITARIA:GESTI\u00d3N SANITARIA refers to the management of health services, emphasizing the importance of efficiency and effectiveness in achieving positive health outcomes while maintaining reasonable costs. This concept encompasses healthcare management, which involves making strategic decisions aimed at optimizing patient care and the allocation of resources within health services."}{"title": "RECURSOS DIAGN\u00d3STICOS Y TERAP\u00c9UTICOS:Diagnostic and therapeutic resources are essential tools in healthcare for patient treatment and management."}{"title": "MEDICINA BASADA EN LA EVIDENCIA:\"MEDICINA BASADA EN LA EVIDENCIA\" (MBE) is a clinical practice approach that emphasizes the integration of the best current evidence with clinical expertise and patient values in making decisions about patient care. This model of medical practice prioritizes the use of the most relevant and up-to-date clinical evidence to inform medical decision-making, ensuring that patient care is both effective and aligned with individual patient needs and preferences."}{"title": "MEDICINA COSTE-EFECTIVA:Cost-effective medicine aims to maximize patient welfare within the constraints of limited resources."}{"title": "RECURSOS SANITARIOS:\"RECURSOS SANITARIOS\" refers to the various resources utilized in healthcare, encompassing all the tools, personnel, materials, and facilities necessary for providing medical care. These resources are essential for effective healthcare delivery and are subject to analysis for cost-effectiveness. The allocation of \"recursos sanitarios\" is crucial in the micro-management of healthcare services, ensuring that the right inputs are available for optimal patient care."}{"title": "MACROGESTI\u00d3N:Macrogesti\u00f3n represents the health policy perspective where the state intervenes to enhance equity and correct market dysfunctions."}{"title": "MESOGESTI\u00d3N:MESOGESTI\u00d3N refers to a management approach that emphasizes the decentralization of management responsibilities to healthcare centers. This strategy aims to enhance service delivery and operational efficiency within the healthcare system. It involves the coordination and motivation of staff within these centers, ensuring that they operate effectively within a regulated environment. By focusing on local management, MESOGESTI\u00d3N seeks to improve the overall quality of healthcare services provided to the community."}{"title": "MICROGESTI\u00d3N:Microgesti\u00f3n refers to the decentralization of management within healthcare settings, empowering individual healthcare professionals to enhance efficiency and accountability. This approach necessitates the active involvement of health center staff, particularly clinicians, who are responsible for making decisions that impact approximately 70% of health resources. By distributing management responsibilities, Microgesti\u00f3n aims to improve the overall effectiveness of healthcare delivery."}{"title": "EEIS:Evaluaci\u00f3n econ\u00f3mica de las intervenciones sanitarias (EEIS) is a process that allows for informed decision-making regarding health interventions based on cost-effectiveness."}{"title": "COSTES SANITARIOS:Costes sanitarios refers to the various costs associated with health services, including structural costs and costs of resources used in therapeutic interventions."}{"title": "COSTES NO SANITARIOS:COSTES NO SANITARIOS refer to the costs incurred by patients that are not directly related to medical services. These costs include expenses associated with transportation, personal care assistance, and other indirect costs linked to health services."}{"title": "CENTRO DE SALUD:Un centro de salud es una instalaci\u00f3n donde se proporciona atenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica y se gestiona la mesogesti\u00f3n de los servicios sanitarios."}{"title": "ASEGURADORA:Una aseguradora es una entidad que proporciona seguros de salud y juega un papel en la mesogesti\u00f3n del sistema sanitario."}{"title": "CALIDAD EN LA ASISTENCIA:La calidad en la asistencia es un objetivo fundamental en la gesti\u00f3n sanitaria, que busca mejorar los resultados de salud."}{"title": "ESTADO:"}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N Y ASPECTOS LEGALES:The entity \"NUTRICI\u00d3N Y ASPECTOS LEGALES\" encompasses a comprehensive examination of the economic and legal dimensions associated with nutrition and healthcare costs. This section highlights the significance of nutrition, alongside the legal considerations pertinent to the research and development of clinical nutrition products. Additionally, it addresses the nutritional analysis and the legal frameworks governing product development, ensuring compliance with European legislation regarding nutrient values. Overall, \"NUTRICI\u00d3N Y ASPECTOS LEGALES\" serves as a critical resource for understanding the interplay between nutrition, legal requirements, and economic factors in the healthcare sector."}{"title": "COSTE IDENTIFICACI\u00d3N:An analysis method that evaluates the cost of a procedure or treatment, particularly when comparing two therapeutic options with identical outcomes"}{"title": "COSTE EFECTIVIDAD:An analysis method used to compare the relative costs and outcomes of different interventions"}{"title": "COSTE UTILIDAD:An analysis method that assesses the cost in relation to the utility gained from a treatment or intervention"}{"title": "COSTE BENEFICIO:An analysis method that compares the costs of an intervention to its benefits, often expressed in monetary terms"}{"title": "COSTE DIRECTO:Direct costs associated with healthcare services, calculated based on established reference prices in a competitive market."}{"title": "COSTE INDIRECTO:Indirect costs related to productivity loss due to morbidity or the cost of replacing lost labor."}{"title": "COSTE TOTAL:The total cost of a clinical process, calculated as the sum of fixed and variable costs."}{"title": "COSTE MEDIO:The average cost of resources used per unit produced in a healthcare setting."}{"title": "COSTE MARGINAL:The cost of producing one additional unit of service or treatment in healthcare."}{"title": "COSTE-UTILIDAD:Coste-utilidad is a type of cost-effectiveness analysis that includes quality of life and life expectancy, allowing comparisons of interventions with different outcomes."}{"title": "COSTE-BENEFICIO:COSTE-BENEFICIO refers to a method of analysis that evaluates the relationship between the costs associated with a particular intervention and the benefits derived from it. This analysis is a complex economic evaluation that examines the cost-benefit relationship in monetary terms, allowing for the comparison of different treatments and their respective outcomes. Through this approach, COSTE-BENEFICIO provides insights into the efficiency and effectiveness of various interventions by quantifying their financial implications."}{"title": "CONTABILIDAD ANALITICA:Contabilidad anal\u00edtica allows for the breakdown of costs of all healthcare resources used in clinical practice, relating them to care activity."}{"title": "A\u00d1OS DE VIDA AJUSTADOS POR CALIDAD:A\u00f1os de vida ajustados por calidad (AVAC) is a metric used to assess the value of medical interventions by considering both the quantity and quality of life gained."}{"title": "ESTUDIOS DE COSTE-EFECTIVIDAD:Estudios de coste-efectividad are research analyses that compare the costs and outcomes of different healthcare interventions to determine their efficiency."}{"title": "DECISIONES ESTRAT\u00c9GICAS:Decisiones estrat\u00e9gicas refer to the choices made in healthcare management based on analyses like cost-effectiveness to optimize resource allocation."}{"title": "MICROGESTI\u00d3N SANITARIA:Microgesti\u00f3n sanitaria involves the detailed management of healthcare resources and interventions at a local level, often informed by cost analyses."}{"title": "POL\u00cdTICA DE LA MESOGESTI\u00d3N:Pol\u00edtica de la mesogesti\u00f3n refers to the mid-level management policies in healthcare that guide resource allocation and intervention strategies."}{"title": "EFECTIVIDAD:Efectividad refers to the success of an intervention in achieving desired health outcomes, a key measure in cost-effectiveness studies."}{"title": "UNIDADES DE NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA:Las Unidades de Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica son centros que se encargan de la atenci\u00f3n nutricional de los pacientes en un entorno hospitalario, evaluando y gestionando su estado nutricional."}{"title": "SISTEMAS DE INFORMACI\u00d3N DE ATENCI\u00d3N ESPECIALIZADA:Los Sistemas de Informaci\u00f3n de Atenci\u00f3n Especializada son herramientas utilizadas para gestionar la actividad hospitalaria y mejorar la atenci\u00f3n al paciente."}{"title": "CMBD:El Conjunto M\u00ednimo B\u00e1sico de Datos (CMBD) es un sistema que contiene datos cl\u00ednicos y administrativos de cada episodio de hospitalizaci\u00f3n, utilizado para la gesti\u00f3n y an\u00e1lisis de la actividad hospitalaria."}{"title": "GRUPOS RELACIONADOS CON EL DIAGN\u00d3STICO:Los Grupos Relacionados con el Diagn\u00f3stico (GRD) son un sistema de clasificaci\u00f3n dise\u00f1ado para agrupar episodios de hospitalizaci\u00f3n de pacientes que presentan caracter\u00edsticas cl\u00ednicas semejantes. Este sistema tiene como objetivo principal evaluar el consumo de recursos en los cuidados hospitalarios, facilitando as\u00ed la gesti\u00f3n eficiente de estos recursos. Al agrupar a los pacientes con caracter\u00edsticas similares, los GRD permiten una mejor organizaci\u00f3n y administraci\u00f3n de los servicios de salud."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LISIS COSTE-EFECTIVIDAD:El an\u00e1lisis coste-efectividad es un procedimiento que permite evaluar la relaci\u00f3n entre los costos y los resultados de diferentes intervenciones m\u00e9dicas."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE DOCUMENTACI\u00d3N M\u00c9DICA:La Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Documentaci\u00f3n M\u00e9dica (SEDOM) se enfoca en la mejora de la documentaci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica y la codificaci\u00f3n en el \u00e1mbito sanitario."}{"title": "CIE-9 MC:La Clasificaci\u00f3n Internacional de Enfermedades, 9\u00aa revisi\u00f3n, Modificaci\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica (CIE-9 MC) es un sistema de codificaci\u00f3n anterior al CIE-10, utilizado para clasificar diagn\u00f3sticos y procedimientos m\u00e9dicos."}{"title": "SERVICIO DE DIGESTIVO:El Servicio de Digestivo es una unidad dentro de un hospital que se especializa en el diagn\u00f3stico y tratamiento de enfermedades del sistema digestivo."}{"title": "MARASMO NUTRICIONAL:Marasmo nutricional is a type of malnutrition resulting from a deficiency in caloric intake, leading to significant weight loss and muscle wasting."}{"title": "DISPOSITIVO DE ALIMENTACI\u00d3N:Dispositivo de alimentaci\u00f3n refers to medical devices used to deliver nutrition directly to the stomach or intestines of patients who cannot eat normally."}{"title": "COSTES DE SERVICIO FUNCIONAL:Costes de servicio funcional involves the financial aspects related to the provision of healthcare services, including the breakdown of costs associated with various healthcare activities."}{"title": "GFH:GFH refers to functional health groups that play a crucial role in organizing, managing, and supporting healthcare activities. These groups are instrumental in the allocation and management of costs associated with healthcare services, ensuring that resources are utilized effectively to enhance the overall efficiency of healthcare delivery."}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N CAL\u00d3RICO-PROTEICA MODERADA:Malnutrici\u00f3n cal\u00f3rico-proteica moderada refers to a moderate level of malnutrition characterized by deficiencies in caloric and protein intake."}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N CAL\u00d3RICO-PROTEICA LEVE:Malnutrici\u00f3n cal\u00f3rico-proteica leve indicates a mild form of malnutrition where there are slight deficiencies in caloric and protein consumption."}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N CAL\u00d3RICO-PROTEICA NO ESPECIFICADA:Malnutrici\u00f3n cal\u00f3rico-proteica no especificada refers to a form of malnutrition that is not clearly defined but involves a lack of both calories and proteins."}{"title": "INTRODUCCI\u00d3N EN VENA PERIF\u00c9RICA:Introducci\u00f3n en vena perif\u00e9rica de sustancia nutricional is a medical procedure for delivering nutritional substances directly into the peripheral veins of patients."}{"title": "INTRODUCCI\u00d3N EN VENA CENTRAL:Introducci\u00f3n en vena central de sustancia nutricional is a procedure for administering nutritional substances directly into the central veins of patients."}{"title": "INTRODUCCI\u00d3N EN BOCA Y FARINGE:Introducci\u00f3n en boca y faringe de sustancia nutricional is a method of delivering nutrition through the mouth and throat, typically for patients who can swallow."}{"title": "INTRODUCCI\u00d3N EN GASTROINTESTINAL SUPERIOR:Introducci\u00f3n en gastrointestinal superior de sustancia nutricional is a procedure for delivering nutrition directly into the upper gastrointestinal tract."}{"title": "INTRODUCCI\u00d3N EN GASTROINTESTINAL INFERIOR:Introducci\u00f3n en gastrointestinal inferior de sustancia nutricional is a method for administering nutrition directly into the lower gastrointestinal tract."}{"title": "INSERCI\u00d3N EN VENA CAVA SUPERIOR:Inserci\u00f3n en vena cava superior de dispositivo de infusi\u00f3n is a medical procedure for placing an infusion device into the superior vena cava for nutritional support."}{"title": "INSERCI\u00d3N EN EST\u00d3MAGO:Inserci\u00f3n en est\u00f3mago de dispositivo de alimentaci\u00f3n is a procedure for placing a feeding device directly into the stomach for nutritional delivery."}{"title": "INSERCI\u00d3N EN YEYUNO:Inserci\u00f3n en yeyuno de dispositivo de alimentaci\u00f3n is a method for placing a feeding device into the jejunum for direct nutritional support."}{"title": "INSERCI\u00d3N EN INTESTINO DELGADO:Inserci\u00f3n en intestino delgado de dispositivo de alimentaci\u00f3n is a procedure for placing a feeding device into the small intestine for nutritional delivery."}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N CAL\u00d3RICO-PROTEICA GRAVE NO ESPECIFICADA:"}{"title": "GESCOT:GESCOT is an information system implemented in many health systems for cost accounting and management."}{"title": "SF:SF stands for service functional, which is responsible for patient care and related costs."}{"title": "URV:URV is a weighted indicator that measures the complexity and resource consumption of units produced by GFH based on cost allocation."}{"title": "INTERCONSULTATIONS:Interconsultations refer to consultations between different healthcare services to provide comprehensive patient care."}{"title": "COST ALLOCATION:Cost allocation is the process of identifying and assigning costs to different services or departments within a healthcare system."}{"title": "CONSEJER\u00cdAS DE SANIDAD:The Health Councils are regional governmental bodies that manage health services and policies within their jurisdictions."}{"title": "SERVICIOS SANITARIOS:Health services refer to the various medical and healthcare services provided to patients, including hospitals and outpatient care."}{"title": "PRESUPUESTO:The budget is a financial plan that quantifies the economic resources allocated for healthcare activities over a defined period."}{"title": "CASE-MIX:Case-mix is a method and system utilized in healthcare management to synthesize clinical processes into a single parameter, allowing for the evaluation of complexity in patient care. It categorizes patients based on the complexity of their conditions and the services they require, facilitating a more organized approach to managing healthcare resources and improving patient outcomes."}{"title": "CONTRATOS DE GESTI\u00d3N:Management contracts are agreements that define the responsibilities and financial arrangements between healthcare providers and funders."}{"title": "OBJETIVOS DE CALIDAD ASISTENCIAL:Quality care objectives are standards set to ensure that healthcare services meet certain quality benchmarks for patient care."}{"title": "INCENTIVOS ECON\u00d3MICOS:Economic incentives are financial rewards provided to healthcare professionals for meeting specific activity and quality objectives."}{"title": "LIMITACIONES DE CONTRATOS:Limitations of contracts refer to the legal and practical challenges associated with management contracts in the healthcare system."}{"title": "UNIDADES DE COMPLEJIDAD HOSPITALARIA:Hospital Complexity Units (UCH) quantify healthcare activity based on case-mix and resource consumption."}{"title": "UNIDADES PONDERADAS DE ASISTENCIA:Weighted Assistance Units (UPA) aim to standardize healthcare activity into a single parameter based on hospitalization days."}{"title": "GESTI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA:Clinical management refers to the organization and administration of healthcare services to ensure quality and efficiency."}{"title": "CALIDAD DE LA ASISTENCIA SANITARIA:Quality of healthcare refers to ensuring that patients receive the most appropriate diagnostic and therapeutic services for optimal health outcomes."}i{0␀␀␀␀␀J}0␀␀␀␀␀~0␀␀␀␀␀÷~0␀␀␀␀␀ô0␀␀␀␀␀ÇÄ0␀␀␀␀␀MÅ0␀␀␀␀␀Ç0␀␀␀␀␀ûÇ0␀␀␀␀␀ˇÇ0␀␀␀␀␀áÉ0␀␀␀␀␀Ñ0␀␀␀␀␀ôÑ0␀␀␀␀␀Ö0␀␀␀␀␀πÖ0␀␀␀␀␀<Ü0␀␀␀␀␀⁄Ü0␀␀␀␀␀oá0␀␀␀␀␀à0␀␀␀␀␀≤à0␀␀␀␀␀Zâ0␀␀␀␀␀â0␀␀␀␀␀ëä0␀␀␀␀␀Wã0␀␀␀␀␀%å0␀␀␀␀␀ç0␀␀␀␀␀é0␀␀␀␀␀∏é0␀␀␀␀␀rè0␀␀␀␀␀^ê0␀␀␀␀␀2ë0␀␀␀␀␀]ë0␀␀␀␀␀!í0␀␀␀␀␀Óí0␀␀␀␀␀Éì0␀␀␀␀␀î0␀␀␀␀␀∏î0␀␀␀␀␀Hï0␀␀␀␀␀·ï0␀␀␀␀␀çñ0␀␀␀␀␀0ó0␀␀␀␀␀·ó0␀␀␀␀␀ìò0␀␀␀␀␀%ô0␀␀␀␀␀∏ô0␀␀␀␀␀ﬂô0␀␀␀␀␀™ö0␀␀␀␀␀@õ0␀␀␀␀␀ú0␀␀␀␀␀bù0␀␀␀␀␀ëû0␀␀␀␀␀Fü0␀␀␀␀␀¯ü0␀␀␀␀␀«†0␀␀␀␀␀ç°0␀␀␀␀␀.¢0␀␀␀␀␀æ¢0␀␀␀␀␀b£0␀␀␀␀␀È£0␀␀␀␀␀è§0␀␀␀␀␀•0␀␀␀␀␀´•0␀␀␀␀␀E¶0␀␀␀␀␀9ß0␀␀␀␀␀ÿß0␀␀␀␀␀Ö®0␀␀␀␀␀F©0␀␀␀␀␀“©0␀␀␀␀␀[™0␀␀␀␀␀Â™0␀␀␀␀␀r´0␀␀␀␀␀¨0␀␀␀␀␀ú¨0␀␀␀␀␀≠0␀␀␀␀␀™≠0␀␀␀␀␀AÆ0␀␀␀␀␀‰Æ0␀␀␀␀␀sØ0␀␀␀␀␀ÛØ0␀␀␀␀␀z∞0␀␀␀␀␀±0␀␀␀␀␀£±0␀␀␀␀␀,≤0␀␀␀␀␀·≤0␀␀␀␀␀ç≥0␀␀␀␀␀#¥0␀␀␀␀␀√¥0␀␀␀␀␀^µ0␀␀␀␀␀Ôµ0␀␀␀␀␀ç∂0␀␀␀␀␀'∑0␀␀␀␀␀N∑0␀␀␀␀␀⁄∑0␀␀␀␀␀K∏0␀␀␀␀␀√π0␀␀␀␀␀#∫0␀␀␀␀␀«∫0␀␀␀␀␀hª0␀␀␀␀␀º0␀␀␀␀␀Øº0␀␀␀␀␀YΩ0␀␀␀␀␀	æ0␀␀␀␀␀≥æ0␀␀␀␀␀Nø0␀␀␀␀␀‹ø0␀␀␀␀␀v¿0␀␀␀␀␀¡0␀␀␀␀␀¨¡0␀␀␀␀␀7¬0␀␀␀␀␀∫¬0␀␀␀␀␀U√0␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ√0␀␀␀␀␀Äƒ0␀␀␀␀␀¸ƒ0␀␀␀␀␀í≈0␀␀␀␀␀5∆0␀␀␀␀␀∫∆0␀␀␀␀␀«0␀␀␀␀␀¢«0␀␀␀␀␀1»0␀␀␀␀␀≤»0␀␀␀␀␀E…0␀␀␀␀␀Ô…0␀␀␀␀␀%Ã0␀␀␀␀␀ÆÃ0␀␀␀␀␀9Õ0␀␀␀␀␀–Õ0␀␀␀␀␀AŒ0␀␀␀␀␀∆Œ0␀␀␀␀␀Pœ0␀␀␀␀␀–œ0␀␀␀␀␀e–0␀␀␀␀␀Ê–0␀␀␀␀␀e—0␀␀␀␀␀¸—0␀␀␀␀␀ä“0␀␀␀␀␀”0␀␀␀␀␀â”0␀␀␀␀␀Û”0␀␀␀␀␀:’0␀␀␀␀␀ø’0␀␀␀␀␀M÷0␀␀␀␀␀ÿ÷0␀␀␀␀␀Z◊0␀␀␀␀␀Õ◊0␀␀␀␀␀[Ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀rŸ0␀␀␀␀␀°Ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀√Ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀⁄0␀␀␀␀␀⁄0␀␀␀␀␀ƒ⁄0␀␀␀␀␀n€0␀␀␀␀␀	‹0␀␀␀␀␀t‹0␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ‹0␀␀␀␀␀]›0␀␀␀␀␀–›0␀␀␀␀␀2ﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀áﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀ﬂ0␀␀␀␀␀Åﬂ0␀␀␀␀␀␀‡0␀␀␀␀␀k‡0␀␀␀␀␀Œ‡0␀␀␀␀␀:·0␀␀␀␀␀è·0␀␀␀␀␀Ú·0␀␀␀␀␀\‚0␀␀␀␀␀¡‚0␀␀␀␀␀!„0␀␀␀␀␀Ñ„0␀␀␀␀␀Ê„0␀␀␀␀␀H‰0␀␀␀␀␀ù‰0␀␀␀␀␀Í‰0␀␀␀␀␀IÂ0␀␀␀␀␀ùÂ0␀␀␀␀␀ÛÂ0␀␀␀␀␀cÊ0␀␀␀␀␀Á0␀␀␀␀␀5Á0␀␀␀␀␀WÁ0␀␀␀␀␀Ë0␀␀␀␀␀≠Ë0␀␀␀␀␀lÈ0␀␀␀␀␀ Í0␀␀␀␀␀öÍ0␀␀␀␀␀Î0␀␀␀␀␀ìÎ0␀␀␀␀␀!Ï0␀␀␀␀␀¢Ï0␀␀␀␀␀#Ì0␀␀␀␀␀ƒÌ0␀␀␀␀␀5Ó0␀␀␀␀␀∞Ó0␀␀␀␀␀-Ô0␀␀␀␀␀±Ô0␀␀␀␀␀"0␀␀␀␀␀ê0␀␀␀␀␀˝0␀␀␀␀␀rÒ0␀␀␀␀␀›Ò0␀␀␀␀␀UÚ0␀␀␀␀␀«Ú0␀␀␀␀␀1Û0␀␀␀␀␀ûÛ0␀␀␀␀␀	Ù0␀␀␀␀␀íÙ0␀␀␀␀␀ı0␀␀␀␀␀vı0␀␀␀␀␀¸ı0␀␀␀␀␀|ˆ0␀␀␀␀␀Úˆ0␀␀␀␀␀b˜0␀␀␀␀␀ˇ˜0␀␀␀␀␀s¯0␀␀␀␀␀Ô¯0␀␀␀␀␀g˘0␀␀␀␀␀€˘0␀␀␀␀␀Q˙0␀␀␀␀␀µ˙0␀␀␀␀␀,˚0␀␀␀␀␀ö˚0␀␀␀␀␀¸0␀␀␀␀␀ì¸0␀␀␀␀␀˝0␀␀␀